  "notes": "Premium SSD and Standard SSD are sold in fixed size tiers, and a disk provisioned at any size in between is billed and served as the next tier up: 200 GiB of Standard SSD is an E15. Performance is therefore a step function of size, which is what makes it possible to state a disk's ceiling from the terraform alone. Premium SSD v2 and Ultra Disk are excluded from this table on purpose: their IOPS and throughput are set independently of size on the resource itself, so the plan already states them and no catalog is needed.",

  "burst_notes": "Premium SSD tiers up to and including P20 (512 GiB) burst to 3,500 IOPS and 170 MB/s on a credit bucket for up to 30 minutes, which is exactly the gp2 trap in a different accent: a benchmark runs on credits and production does not. P30 and larger support on-demand bursting, which is billed rather than banked and has no duration limit.",

