  "standard_ssd_notes": "Standard SSD figures are documented as 'up to', not as provisioned guarantees: Microsoft designs them to deliver the stated numbers 99% of the time rather than 99.9%. A rule must not present them as a floor. Every tier from E1 to E50 shares the same 500 IOPS and 100 MB/s, which is the point worth making: buying a bigger Standard SSD buys capacity and nothing else until E60."
